WEBVTT

00:03:58.356 --> 00:04:01.381
He promised, "It's not how
we'll do things in the future,

00:04:01.405 --> 00:04:03.335
but it's how we have to do them today."

00:04:04.504 --> 00:04:06.362
John wasn't wrong on either count.

00:04:07.061 --> 00:04:09.300
Meetings before the meeting
are a necessary evil

00:04:09.324 --> 00:04:10.475
in his company today,

00:04:10.499 --> 00:04:12.014
and I didn't like it at all.

00:04:12.739 --> 00:04:16.148
Sure, it was going
to be inefficient and annoying,

00:04:16.172 --> 00:04:18.356
but what bothered me most
was his confidence

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:20.748
that it's not how
they'll do things in the future.

00:04:21.323 --> 00:04:22.663
How could he be sure?

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:26.923
Who was going to change it and when,
if it wasn't him and now?

00:04:27.994 --> 00:04:29.349
What would the trigger be?

00:04:29.373 --> 00:04:30.616
And when it happened,